    "summary": "Electrifying second set with soaring jams and Hornsby flair",
    "blurb": "The show shines on the second half, featuring a fiery Foolish Heart, Terrapin Station and a soaring Let It Grow > Jam > Valley Road sequence. Jerry’s tone is immaculate while Bruce Hornsby adds a bust‑out keyboard texture. The encore closes with an emotional rendition of The Weight.",
    "review": "On October 30, 1990 at Wembley Arena the Dead delivered one of those rare Fall ’90 shows that still feels fresh after all these years. The first set stumbled a bit with a mix imbalance, but by the time they launched into Jack Straw and the seamless Let It Grow > Jam > Valley Road trio the band was fully in its stride. Highlights include a soaring Foolish Heart, a beautifully layered Terrapin Station, and an inspiring Wheel transition driven by tight drumming. Bruce Hornsby’s keyboards were a standout‑plus, bursting out on the jams and adding texture that lifted the whole performance. Despite a slightly strained vocal from Jerry toward the end, Bob stepped up front and the encore’s The Weight landed with genuine emotion, making this a must‑listen show for any Deadhead.\n\nThe soundboard capture (gd90-10-30.dsbd.barbella.6678.sbeok.shnf) is the clear winner – crisp, well‑balanced and faithful to the band’s dynamic energy. For those who prefer a bit more ambience, the excellent matrix recordings also deliver a vivid live feel, but none match the clarity of the recommended SBD source.",
